* opamp_core input common-mode range (ICMR) testbench -- circuit BODY for `klt sim` (issue #53)
*
* A `klt sim` circuit body (no .control, no .end, no .lib/.temp: klt generates
* the wrapper, the per-corner `.lib` / `.temp` / `alter vdd` cards and the
* analysis card; the `.meas` cards live in the request -- see klayout-tools
* docs/cli/sim.md "Netlist convention"). bin/pvt_sweep.py renders the few
* placeholders below, writes the request JSON beside it and submits the grid
* (one request per VDD group, `--backend batch` by default). Never run
* directly. Measurements are `.meas` cards only -- the fleet's klt (0.5.0) has
* no `measurements[].expr`, so no device-parameter (@m.x..[vdsat]) probing is
* possible; see the README for what that costs.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------- topology
* Why not the unity-gain follower of opamp_dc_swing.spice.tmpl: there the
* output equals the input, so the swept common-mode voltage IS the output
* voltage and an edge can be an input-stage limit or an output-compliance
* limit with no way to tell which (that bench's own header says it is "not
* an independent measurement of the input-common-mode range"). This bench
* holds the OUTPUT at mid-rail while the input common mode is swept:
*
*   inverting unity-gain loop (Rin = Rf), both amplifier inputs at the
*   swept common-mode voltage Vcm = v(inp):
*       Bsrc forces  v(src) = 2*Vcm - VDD/2
*       inn  = (src + out)/2
*   => out - VDD/2 = 2*(inn - Vcm) = 2*vid, with vid = v(inn) - v(inp).
*   While the loop has gain, out stays within a few vid of VDD/2 for EVERY
*   Vcm, so the output stage never moves and a change of vid can only come
*   from the INPUT stage: vid(Vcm) is the input-referred offset shift caused
*   by the common-mode voltage (= the CM-induced output shift divided by the
*   loop's open-loop gain). Rin = Rf = 100 k keeps the
*   resistor current (< ~ +-10 uA) far below the class-A output sink.
*
*   Two copies of the amplifier share the deck (the flat xschem netlist is
*   wrapped in a local .subckt, as in opamp_cmrr.spice.tmpl):
*     S1  at the swept common mode  Vcm      (inp1 = Vinp, the DC sweep variable)
*     S2  at                        Vcm + dV (inp2 = v(inp1) + dV, dV = {DV} V)
*   so v(k) = |vid2 - vid1| / dV = |d vid / d Vcm| is the LOCAL common-mode
*   sensitivity (input-referred shift per volt of common mode) at every Vcm
*   of one DC sweep, i.e. 1 / (local DC CMRR). Inside the input stage's
*   operating range it is small (1/CMRR, ~ -55 to -71 dB at mid-supply,
*   measured by opamp_cmrr.spice.tmpl); at the ends of the range the tail
*   current source / input pair leave saturation and it rises by orders of
*   magnitude within a few tens of mV -- a sharp knee, so the edge is not very
*   sensitive to the threshold (checked by the 30 / 40 / 50 dB band below).
*
* ------------------------------------------------------- ICMR criterion
* Fixed in this file's first commit, before any batch result existed (the
* README "ICMR bench" section carries the same statement and its caveat).
* ICMR at one (corner, temperature) point is the contiguous range of Vcm
* containing Vcm = VDD/2 over which
*       local DC CMRR  =  1 / |d vid / d Vcm|   >=  40 dB   (primary),   0 <= Vcm <= VDD
* with the output held at mid-rail the whole time (so output-stage limits
* are excluded by construction). 30 dB and 50 dB are reported as a
* sensitivity band, measured in the same run as other `v(k)` crossing levels.
* v(k) below adds 1 (= 0 dB CMRR) outside [0, VDD] so a crossing always
* exists at the rails: an edge at <= 0 V / >= VDD means "no input-stage
* limit before the rail", and the edge value is then the rail.
* Edges are `.meas dc ... when v(k)=LEVEL` crossings (linearly interpolated
* between 5 mV sweep points), the nearest crossing below and above mid-supply.
* Honest caveat (README): this is a CMRR-degradation definition of the range,
* not a device-saturation one -- the fleet's klt (0.5.0) cannot probe
* @m.x..[vdsat], so which device leaves saturation is not recorded.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------ shared conventions
* ibias / Iref = 5 uA reference and CL = 2 pF as opamp_ac.spice.tmpl; the
* netlist under test is the same flat xschem netlist. The MOS process corner
* AND the typical R+C corner both come from the `.lib <sky130.lib.spice>
* <corner>` section klt appends (that section itself includes corners/<c>.spice
* plus r+c/res_typical__cap_typical.spice and its __lin sibling -- the
* identical files the ngspice-loop benches include by hand).

.option scale=1u
.option reltol=1e-6 vntol=1e-9 abstol=1e-14

.subckt opamp_dut vdd vss inn inp out ibias
.include "{OPAMP_NETLIST}"
.ends opamp_dut

Vdd vdd 0 dc {VDD_NOM}
Vss vss 0 dc 0
* supply-current sense for copy S1 only (0 V source)
Vsense vdd vdd_1 dc 0

* S1: swept copy at Vcm
Iref_1 vdd_1 ibias_1 dc {IBIAS_A}
Vinp inp_1 0 dc 0
Bsrc_1 src_1 0 V = 2*v(inp_1) - 0.5*v(vdd)
Rin_1 src_1 inn_1 {RLOOP}
Rf_1 inn_1 out_1 {RLOOP}
Cload_1 out_1 0 {CL_F}
X1 vdd_1 vss inn_1 inp_1 out_1 ibias_1 opamp_dut

* S2: copy at Vcm + dV
Iref_2 vdd ibias_2 dc {IBIAS_A}
Binp_2 inp_2 0 V = v(inp_1) + {DV}
Bsrc_2 src_2 0 V = 2*v(inp_2) - 0.5*v(vdd)
Rin_2 src_2 inn_2 {RLOOP}
Rf_2 inn_2 out_2 {RLOOP}
Cload_2 out_2 0 {CL_F}
X2 vdd vss inn_2 inp_2 out_2 ibias_2 opamp_dut

* convergence aid (added after the first fleet attempt, before any ICMR figure
* was accepted): the fleet's ngspice-46 stalled for >600 s in gmin/source
* stepping at some sweep points of the tt/sf/fs 1.8 V group. Seed the loop
* nodes at mid-rail; a .nodeset only guides the first iteration, it does not
* change the converged solution.
.nodeset v(out_1)={NS_MID} v(inn_1)={NS_MID} v(out_2)={NS_MID} v(inn_2)={NS_MID}

Bvid1 vid1 0 V = v(inn_1) - v(inp_1)
Bk k 0 V = abs((v(inn_2) - v(inp_2)) - v(vid1)) / {DV} + u(-v(inp_1)) + u(v(inp_2) - v(vdd))
